  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: diocese</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The Diocese of Pontus was a diocese of the later Roman Empire. It was established in 314. Justinian would abolish the diocese in 535/6, only to re-establish it in 548. This diocese would continue to function until it was replaced by the themata of Armeniakon and Opsikion in the seventh century.",
